@startuml
title FSM - Conditionals: Hysteresis, Latching and Flag Bridges

skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide empty members

' Cross-diagram references (see uml-state.puml)
package "FSM" {
  class "ConditionalCallback<T>" as ConditionalCallbackT
  class "State<T>" as StateT
  class Flag
}

package "FSM" {
  class "FlagSetCondition<T>" as FlagSetConditionT {
    # flag : Flag*
    # childCallback(comp, val, ref)
  }

  class BangBangConditional {
    - state : bool
    - triggered : bool
    - low : Number
    - high : Number
    - rising : void*
    - falling : void*
    # childReference(val) : Number
    # childCallback(comp, val, ref)
    # callOperator(val, ref)
  }

  class LatchingConditional {
    - state : bool
    - triggered : bool
    - rising : void*
    - falling : void*
    # childReference(val) : bool
    # childCallback(comp, val, ref)
    # callOperator(val, ref)
  }

  class BangBangFlagSet {
    - state : bool
    - triggered : bool
    - low : Number
    - high : Number
    # childReference(val) : Number
    # childCallback(comp, val, ref)
    # callOperator(val, ref)
  }

  class LatchingFlagSet {
    - state : bool
    - triggered : bool
    # childReference(val) : bool
    # childCallback(comp, val, ref)
    # callOperator(val, ref)
  }
}

FlagSetConditionT --|> ConditionalCallbackT
BangBangConditional --|> ConditionalCallbackT : ConditionalCallback<Number>
LatchingConditional --|> ConditionalCallbackT : ConditionalCallback<bool>
BangBangFlagSet --|> FlagSetConditionT : FlagSetCondition<Number>
LatchingFlagSet --|> FlagSetConditionT : FlagSetCondition<bool>

FlagSetConditionT --> Flag : sets

StateT ..> FlagSetConditionT : creates
StateT ..> BangBangConditional : creates\n(addLatchingConditional Number)
StateT ..> LatchingConditional : creates\n(addLatchingConditional bool)
StateT ..> BangBangFlagSet : creates\n(addLatchingSetFlag Number/time)
StateT ..> LatchingFlagSet : creates\n(addLatchingSetFlag bool)

note right of FlagSetConditionT
Bridge condition: compare source state, then write result to Flag.
Use to convert threshold logic into stable boolean control signals.
Derived classes specialize hysteresis and latching behavior.
end note

note right of BangBangConditional
Numeric hysteresis comparator with high/low thresholds.
Triggers on edge crossings and suppresses chatter near boundaries.
Typical use: thermostat or debounce-like threshold control.
end note

note right of LatchingConditional
Boolean edge latch.
Alternates internal expectation after each successful trigger,
so callbacks fire on transitions rather than steady levels.
end note

note right of BangBangFlagSet
Hysteresis-to-flag adapter.
Implements bang-bang threshold tracking, then sets target Flag.
Designed for robust actuator toggling from analog-style inputs.
end note

note right of LatchingFlagSet
Boolean latch-to-flag adapter.
Converts alternating true/false events into deterministic Flag writes.
Useful when control flow needs explicit edge-driven toggles.
end note

@enduml
